\nGodot already has 5k issues, so reporting this issue might be pointless as it just gets added to the gigantic mountain of unresolved, unlooked at issues. But making this post will cause it to appear in SEO and possibly be helpful to some people.\n\nAs the title says, typing an array causes it to always be empty after setting it with values.\n\nCode: \n\n```GDScript\n# the erroring code:\nvar placeholder_card: Types_.Card = Types_.Card.new(\n\t\"placeholder\", # name\n\t1, # energy cost\n\t1, # attack\n\t10 # health\n)\nvar works_as_expected = [PetCards_.placeholder_card.duplicate(true)]\nvar is_always_empty: Array[Types_.Card] = [PetCards_.placeholder_card.duplicate(true)]\n\n# the Card class:\nclass Card extends Resource:\n\tvar name: String\n\tvar energy_cost: int\n\tvar attack: int\n\tvar health: int\n\tvar connected_node: CardNode\n\tfunc _init(p_name: String, p_energy_cost: int, p_attack: int, p_health: int):\n\t\tname = p_name\n\t\tenergy_cost = p_energy_cost\n\t\tattack = p_attack\n\t\thealth = p_health\n```\n\nClearly, this is a bug. Or if it's the \"expected behavior\", then it's a design bug and is still an issue. (Whenever devs talk about \"expected behavior\", what they really mean is that it's expected to them, but not to anybody else. People who use the term use it because they have failed to empathize with their users. Devs ought to remove this terminology from their memories permanently.)\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11, Godot 4.3\n\n### Issue description\n\nSee above.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nSee above.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nAll you need to do is run the code above. There is no need to provide an entire project.","closed_by":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/u